    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on a high-ceiling matchup today, spearheaded by **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the squad with an elite 79.74 projection. Batting leadoff against Kremer, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an optimized platoon advantage and favorable order placement, making him the anchor of our lineup. Following closely is **Jacob Wilson** (65.32) and **Andy Pages** (63.46). **Jacob Wilson** thrives today due to a favorable park environment and strong SP skill metrics, while **Andy Pages** is bolstered by a wind-aided outfield and a productive spot in the two-hole against Cameron. Despite facing a tough arm in Henderson, **Jackson Merrill** maintains a solid floor of 50.37, as his dynamic platoon advantage helps offset the difficult matchup against a sub-3.00 xERA pitcher.\n\nThe decision to bench **Wade Meckler** at 35.04 was the most difficult call of the day. While **Wade Meckler** offers the speed profile we covet, his neutral platoon disadvantage against Gore and a bottom-of-the-order assignment suppressed his output below our strict 40.0 efficiency floor, leading us to favor the higher projected volume of **Luis Lara**. We are also closely monitoring **Drake Baldwin**; while his 54.36 score is respectable, he carries a 37% rain risk that could compromise his game cap efficiency. With **Jordan Westburg** sidelined on the IL and both **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** unavailable, the Waves must rely on this core to maximize R and RBI production today. We are playing for consistent contact and high-leverage plate appearances, especially as we look for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (60.95) to drive the middle of the order against a beatable Gray.",
